{block content}
<h1>Find your kind of game</h1><p class="text-body-secondary mb-4">Start with the kind of evening you have in mind. There is no need to stick to just one genre.</p>
<ul class="nav nav-tabs" id="genreTabs" role="tablist">
    <li class="nav-item" role="presentation"><button class="nav-link active" id="story-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-bs-target="#story" type="button" role="tab" aria-controls="story" aria-selected="true">Story &amp; exploration</button></li>
    <li class="nav-item" role="presentation"><button class="nav-link" id="challenge-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-bs-target="#challenge" type="button" role="tab" aria-controls="challenge" aria-selected="false">A little challenge</button></li>
    <li class="nav-item" role="presentation"><button class="nav-link" id="relaxed-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-bs-target="#relaxed" type="button" role="tab" aria-controls="relaxed" aria-selected="false">A slower evening</button></li>
</ul>
<div class="tab-content border border-top-0 rounded-bottom p-3 p-md-4 mb-5">
    <section class="tab-pane fade show active" id="story" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="story-tab" tabindex="0"><h2 class="h4">Go somewhere else for a while.</h2><p>Adventure games focus on places, characters and discovery. RPGs add decisions about your character, equipment and the way you approach a situation.</p><div class="row g-3"><div class="col-md-6"><h3 class="h6">Adventure</h3><p class="text-body-secondary">Firewatch follows a conversation across a remote forest. Outer Wilds turns exploration into a mystery that rewards curiosity.</p></div><div class="col-md-6"><h3 class="h6">Role-playing</h3><p class="text-body-secondary">Baldur's Gate 3 offers party-based choices and turn-based battles. The Witcher 3 combines exploration with character-driven quests.</p></div></div></section>
    <section class="tab-pane fade" id="challenge" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="challenge-tab" tabindex="0"><h2 class="h4">Try, learn, try again.</h2><p>Action games test timing and reactions, while puzzle and strategy games ask you to stop and think. Both can make a small breakthrough feel rewarding.</p><div class="row g-3"><div class="col-md-6"><h3 class="h6">Action &amp; platformers</h3><p class="text-body-secondary">Hades changes the tools available on each run. Celeste builds precise platforming around short rooms and quick retries.</p></div><div class="col-md-6"><h3 class="h6">Puzzles &amp; strategy</h3><p class="text-body-secondary">Portal 2 asks you to rethink space. Slay the Spire asks you to build a deck and work with the choices you are given.</p></div></div></section>
    <section class="tab-pane fade" id="relaxed" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="relaxed-tab" tabindex="0"><h2 class="h4">Set your own pace.</h2><p>Simulation and sandbox games give you systems to explore and room to choose your own goals. A session can be as small as finishing a field or improving one corner of a factory.</p><div class="row g-3"><div class="col-md-6"><h3 class="h6">Simulation</h3><p class="text-body-secondary">Stardew Valley mixes farming with village life. Euro Truck Simulator 2 is about planning deliveries and spending time on the road.</p></div><div class="col-md-6"><h3 class="h6">Building &amp; sandbox</h3><p class="text-body-secondary">Terraria lets you explore and build in a 2D world. Satisfactory turns resource gathering into a growing network of machines.</p></div></div></section>
</div>
<a n:href="games" class="btn btn-primary">Explore the game library</a>
